Let $\cc{O}_K = \Z[\zeta_3]$ be the ring of integers of $K$. \\
Let $\cc{O}^\times_K$ be the group of units of $\cc{O}_K$. \\
Let $\zeta_3 \in K$ be any primitive third root of unity. \\
Let $\eta \in \cc{O}_K$ be the element corresponding to $\zeta_3 \in K$. \\
Let $\lambda \in \cc{O}_K$ be such that $\lambda = \eta -1$. \\\\
Then $\lambda \divides 3$. -/
TheoremDoc IsCyclotomicExtension.Rat.Three.lambda_dvd_three as "lambda_dvd_three" in "Third Cyclotomic Extensions"

Statement lambda_dvd_three : λ ∣ 3 := by
  Hint "By properties of norms and divisibility, if the norm of an element in the ring of integers
divides a number, then the element itself must divide that number.
In this case, by *lmm:norm_lambda* we know that the norm of $\\lambda$ is $3$, that divides $3$,
which implies that $\\lambda \\divides 3$."
  suffices λ ∣ (3 : ℤ) by simpa
  rw [← Ideal.norm_dvd_iff, _root_.IsCyclotomicExtension.Rat.Three.norm_lambda hζ]
  rw [_root_.IsCyclotomicExtension.Rat.Three.norm_lambda hζ]
  exact Int.prime_three

